3. **The two router-level gates, letter-case proof** (`app.use('/api/feedback', ...)` `:21981`, `app.use('/api/sustainability', ...)` `:22051`): add, in `server.js` ahead of each router, a small gate function that applies `requireAdminFor` to `PATCH` and `DELETE` on one item path (feedback: `/^\/[^/]+\/?$/`) and to `POST` on the config path (sustainability: `/^\/config\/?$/i`), matched on `req.path` **case-insensitively** (the `i` flag on both), with the comment that the match follows Express's own routing (any letter case, one optional trailing slash). `routes/feedback.js` and `routes/sustainability.js` are NOT edited. **The case-insensitive match is an explicit cell, not a side effect: cells CASE-1 to CASE-5 below.** Q3 of the report offers the structural alternative (gate inside the routers so routing and gating cannot disagree) and its partition cost; the default is the placement above.
